    "body": "@inikulin Depends on the implementation. As far as I understand from parse5 code, it does, but in our in-house implementations \"reconsume\" means just \"don't do anything and go to specified state\" (in opposite to regular character consumption where you actually move pointer), so it cleans up code without any performance penalty at all. I believe parse5 wouldn't be hard to change this way as well.\n",
